== Strengths

The current design was able to successfully adhere an MPHX plate to a lamina in testing. This means in particular that it was able to have sufficiently precise lamina alignment (requirement 5), and a form factor which fits within a fume hood. This means that overall the design was successful in its core goal of adhering MPHX plates to laminae. The calculations done in Appendix III also indicate that the design is mechanically sound and can withstand well beyond the required 1000 MPHX plates.

== Weaknesses

A major issue with the design currently is chemical adhesive compatibility. Currently, using PC MPHX plates and PC film, the adhesion between the plate and film is not especially high. This is because we had originally designed the system for use with ABS plates and PC film, but the injection molding company had to switch to PC film in the middle of the quarter due to manufacturing quality issues. We did not perform the formal adhesive strength test (Requirement 1) due to this issue.


== Future Work

Future testing and improvements will likely require the MPHX injection-molding manufacturing process to be fully stable to prevent last-minute design changes discussed in the previous section.

Assuming the current design is still active, future teams should consider pairing the PC MPHX plates with an ABS film, since the adhesive we selected was optimized for PC-ABS bonding. This film should preferably be 400 microns thick and flat; any bowing will cause alignment issues. A successfully glued MPHX plate can then be pressure-tested to verify it has specific adhesion.

